meta {
  name: 03 Invoices
  seq: 3
}

docs {
  # Finance → Invoices

  Invoice list + lifecycle (`/finance/invoices`; All / Pending / Partial /
  Completed / Overdue / Cancelled). **Backend-wired** via the `invoice` module.

  Invoices are created ONLY from selected outstanding order records (see
  **01 Reports/03 Outstanding**). The create endpoint takes a `partyType` (one of
  the four invoiceable panels — B2B / Referred By / Internal Referral User /
  External Referral User) plus `sourceOrderIds`; the server re-derives the gross
  amount and party from those orders (never trusting body amounts), enforces
  same-party, rejects already-invoiced orders, and derives TDS/net. Completion rule
  is "Invoice Amount Only": an invoice is Completed once its net amount is fully
  received (outstanding TDS is tracked separately).

  Endpoints (all under `/invoices`):
  - `POST /invoices` — create from source orders
  - `GET /invoices` — list (filters + pagination)
  - `GET /invoices/summary` — the seven summary-card totals
  - `GET /invoices/:id` — one invoice + source orders + payments
  - `GET /invoices/:id/payments` — payment history
  - `POST /invoices/:id/receive-payment` — record an INVOICE or TDS receipt
  - `POST /invoices/:id/cancel` — cancel with a reason (blocked once paid)

  Run **Business Auth → Login** first so `businessAccessToken` is populated, and set
  `invoiceId` (from a create response) + `orderId` (an outstanding order of one
  party) as collection/environment vars.
}
